# Auto deploy after changes

When the agent finishes a set of code/style changes the user asked for, do **all** of the following before ending the turn (unless the user says not to deploy):

1. **Commit** only the relevant changed files (no secrets, no `backups/`, no unrelated junk).
2. **Push** the current branch to `origin` (`git push -u origin HEAD` if needed).
3. **Deploy** to production host from env (see below):
   - Path: `/opt/render-screen`
   - `git fetch` + checkout current branch + `git reset --hard origin/<branch>`
   - `git rev-parse --short HEAD > .git-commit`
   - `docker compose build app && docker compose up -d --force-recreate app nginx`
   - Verify `https://screen.norenvpn.com/api/health`
4. **Restart local** `npm run dev` on `PORT` from `.env` (default 3001) if it was running or the user uses local preview.

## Credentials (never commit, never print)

Read from `.env` (gitignored):

- `DEPLOY_HOST` (e.g. `144.31.218.222`)
- `DEPLOY_USER` (e.g. `root`)
- `DEPLOY_SSH_PASSWORD` (or SSH key if BatchMode works)
- `DEPLOY_PATH` (default `/opt/render-screen`)
- `DEPLOY_BRANCH` (optional; default = current git branch)

Helper: `python scripts/_deploy_remote.py` (reads `.env`, no secrets in repo).
Must stream remote logs live (`[deploy] 1/4…4/4`) — do not buffer until exit.

If SSH key auth fails, use Paramiko with `DEPLOY_SSH_PASSWORD`. Do not echo the password in chat or logs.

## Notes

- Server `update.sh` may fail on interactive `git pull`; prefer `fetch` + `reset --hard origin/<branch>`.
- Skip deploy only for pure questions / docs-only answers with no runnable change.
